{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>We remember the fish.</b> When the Nile spreads in its usual manner and afterward returns to its place, the fish remain in pools in the marshes, and their women draw water from those marshes and the fish enter their pitchers. And so the Sages said." "<b>Which we ate in Egypt for free.</b> Without labor and without cost." "<b>The cucumbers and the melons.</b> To eat at the end of the meal." "<b>The leeks and the onions.</b> To season the pot together with the meat." "<b>The garlic.</b> To dip the meat and the fish."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:21.405071610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}